# Cypress Self-Healer

A Claude Code agent that fixes **one** failing Cypress spec. It runs the spec in Chrome, reads the real page where the test fails, finds the cause, and proposes a small fix to a selector or a wait. It never changes what the test checks.

Agent file: `.claude/agents/cypress-self-healer.md`
Page-scan tool: `.claude/agents/tools/dom-digest.js`

---

## When to use it

| Situation | Use |
|---|---|
| You know which spec is broken | **cypress-self-healer** |
| A spec is flaky (passes one run, fails the next) | **cypress-self-healer** |
| The frontend changed (new column, renamed button) and some tests broke | **cypress-self-healer** |
| You want to fix what failed in last night's Jenkins run | `cypress-report-healer`, or `/cypress-nightlyreportaudit` first |

The report-healer chooses which specs to fix and in which order. The self-healer does the fixing, one spec at a time.

